TION DE TYPE OUVERT NON EQUILIBRE</invention-title><citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="JP-58025309-A" status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>58025309</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="A"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-4471095-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>4471095</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1161982A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>JAPAN SCIENCE &amp; TECH CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUNO KOICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>JAPAN SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUNO, KOICHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUNO KOICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUNO, KOICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A flow reactor for liquid-phase polymerization reactions. A liquid reaction mixture containing organic reactant molecules to be polymerized is jetted into a low-temperature high-pressure part (B) from a high-temperature high-pressure part (A) through a circulation line (C) to inhibit the polymer yielded in the part (A) from decomposing in the part (B). The polymer is sent to the part (A) through a circulation line (C) to further cause polymerization. This cycle is repeated. Thus, a reaction such as amino acid polymerization can be conducted in a nonequilibrium open system while regulating the degree of polymerization by controlling polymerization and decomposition.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un réacteur à circulation destiné à provoquer des réactions de polymérisation en phase liquide. On projette un mélange réactionnel liquide contenant des molécules organiques réactives à polymériser dans une partie à haute pression et basse température (B) depuis une partie à haute pression et haute température (A) via un tube de circulation (C) afin d'empêcher le polymère produit dans la partie (A) de se décomposer dans la partie (B). Le polymère précité est envoyé dans la partie (A) à travers un tube de circulation (C) afin de poursuivre la polymérisation. Ce cycle se reproduit à plusieurs reprises. De cette manière, on parvient à effectuer une réaction telle que la polymérisation d'acides aminés dans un système ouvert non équilibré, le degré de polymérisation étant réglé grâce à une régulation de la polymérisation et de la décomposition.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>